From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:38:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: make g16_fw_cached a bitmask of
 command-object kinds

The macOS driver maps its queue objects, job blocks and work records
cacheable for the firmware. g16_fw_cached switched every command object
at once, so a boot that went wrong could not say which kind did it.

Make it a bitmask of kinds: 0x1 queue objects (queue info, scheduler
contexts, job lists, the registration barrier), 0x2 compute commands
(work image, sequence object, barrier), 0x4 render TA (work image,
sequence), 0x8 render FS (work image, sequence, the pass slot's
barriers) and 0x10 the queues' work rings. The receipt reads only the
uncached cursors when queue objects are cached, as it did before for the
whole switch.

The value 1 now selects queue objects only. The default of 0 keeps every
kind uncached.

Assisted-by: LLM
